            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0497" n="487" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg487"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-07T16:00:00+08:00">October 7, 1948—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 7—6:30 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>279. KMA at Chinwangtao reported noon today tension steadily increasing
                    Shanhaikuan as city reported under fire and shells have fallen within walls;
                    also stated situation Chinwangtao shows signs of deteriorating.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 506, repeated Shanghai 485, Peiping, Mukden and Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
